[T2,T3,T4] (Bamboo), and hand has W6 \u2014 if I discard W6, I lose the third suit (Characters), so All Types impossible.  \n\nGiven melds are Dots and Bamboo, if I keep W6, I have all three suits for All Types? Yes: W6 (Characters), T\u2019s (Bamboo), B\u2019s (Dots), and need winds/dragons \u2014 I have none in hand, but melds have none either. So All Types needs wind/dragon in hand or melds. Not present.  \n\nSo maybe simpler: aim for **All Chows** (four chows + pair) \u2014 I already have 2 chows melded, hand has potential for two more chows: T3,T4,T5 and T5,T6,T7 or B5,B6,B7.  \n\nBut T5 conflict: I can only use it once.  \n\nBetter: discard T5 or T6 or T7 to break the overlap?  \n\nIf I discard T5, then T3,T4 need T2 or T5 for chow \u2014 but T2 is gone (1 left unshown), risky.  \n\nIf I discard T3, then T4,T5,T6 could be chow if I get T3 or T7? Wait T4,T5,T6 is a chow already (I have T4,T5,T6 in hand) \u2014 yes, that\u2019s a chow. Then T6,T7 need T5 or T8. But T5 is in hand (1 left after using in T4,T5,T6 chow) \u2014 so T6,T7 can\u2019t form chow without drawing.  \n\nActually: current hand: T3,T4,T5,T6,T7 \u2192 possible chow sets:  \nSet A: (T3,T4,T5) + (T6,T7, need T8)  \nSet B: (T4,T5,T6) + (T3,T7, not possible) or (T5,T6,T7) + (T3,T4, need T2 or T5)  \n\nBest: keep T4,T5,T6 chow and T3,T7 as terminals needing T2 or T5 or T8.  \n\nBut T3 is less useful alone.  \n\nGiven game stage (many tiles discarded), safe discard is important.  \n\nFrom history, T6 not discarded much, T5 discarded by prev player once (Play T5), T7 not discarded.  \n\nBut T6 is in my hand, and unshown 4 left \u2014 maybe keep for pair potential.  \n\nDiscard W6 is safe (W suit discarded often) and improves hand consistency.  \n\n**Final choice: discard W6** to keep hand more suited-oriented and preserve T/B sequences.  \n\n**Reason:**  \nW6 is isolated from my two melds (both are T and B suits). Discarding it increases hand uniformity, keeps all T and B tiles which can form chows and pairs more easily. Unshown tiles for W6 are 3 left, but W suit is being discarded by others, so relatively safe. Keeping T3,T4,T5,T6,T7,B5,B6 allows multiple chow possibilities and pair chances with T6 or B6 (4 left each).  \n\n**Answer:** Play W6"}
